hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"21413","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, saying: Zuhayr and Ibn Idris narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Ishaq from Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Mamar ibn Abi Habibah from Ubayd ibn Rifah ibn Rafi from his father, Zuhayr saying in his hadith: Rifah ibn Rafi, and he was an Aqabi Badri, who said: I was with Umar when it was said to him: Zayd ibn Thabit gives fatwa to people in the mosque, Zuhayr saying in his hadith: people by his opinion concerning one who has intercourse and does not ejaculate, so he said: Hasten him to me, so he was brought, and he said: O enemy of yourself, have you reached that you give fatwa to people in the mosque of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) by your opinion. He said: I did not do it, but my paternal uncles narrated to me from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Which of your uncles. He said: Ubayy ibn Kab, Zuhayr saying: and Abu Ayyub and Rifah ibn Rafi. So I turned to what this youth says, Zuhayr saying: what this boy says, and I said: We used to do it in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Did you ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about it. He said: We used to do it in his time and we did not wash. So he gathered the people, and the people agreed that water is only from water, except two men, Ali ibn Abi Talib and Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: When the circumcised passes the circumcised, ghusl has become obligatory. He said: Ali said: O Commander of the Believers, the most knowledgeable of people concerning this are the wives of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he sent to Hafsah and she said: I have no knowledge. So he sent to Aishah and she said: When the circumcised passes the circumcised, ghusl is obligatory. He said: Umar was enraged, meaning he became angry, then said: It shall not reach me that anyone did it and does not wash except I punish him severely."
"21414","Abdullah narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Abd al-Ala ibn Abd al-Ala narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Ishaq from Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Mamar ibn Habibah from Ubayd ibn Rifah ibn Rafi from his father, and he mentioned similar to it and its meaning."
